sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Renderer startup sequence
    accDescr: RD backends create a device, OpenGL establishes a context, and headless selects dummy rendering before server construction.
    participant Main
    participant Display as DisplayServer
    participant Context as RenderingContextDriver
    participant RD as RenderingDevice
    participant GL as Platform GL context manager
    participant Server as RenderingServerDefault
    participant Comp as Compositor factory
    Main->>Main: Select method and driver
    Main->>Display: Create display server
    alt RD backend
        Display->>Context: Initialize and create surface
        Display->>RD: Initialize with context and window
        RD->>Context: Create native device driver
        Display->>Comp: Select RendererCompositorRD
    else OpenGL / OpenGL ES
        Display->>GL: Establish native context
        Display->>Comp: Select RasterizerGLES3
    else Headless
        Display->>Comp: Select RasterizerDummy
    end
    Main->>Server: Construct and init
    Server->>Server: Enter required render thread
    Server->>Comp: Create component family
    Comp-->>Server: Storage and drawing interfaces
    Server->>Server: Publish RSG and attach scene renderer
